[112.769659, "i", "cat > /home/user/ops/FIX_SUMMARY.md << 'EOF'\n# Cleanup Script Fix Summary\n\n## Problem\nThe purge_old_runs.py script was running nightly via cron and exiting successfully (exit 0),\nbut was not actually deleting old experiment runs. Disk usage remained at 81-82% despite\nthe script claiming to process files.\n\n## Root Causes Identified\n\n### Bug 1: Wrong deletion method (Line 58)\n**Issue**: Used `os.remove()` instead of `shutil.rmtree()`\n- `os.remove()` only works on FILES, not directories\n- Each run is a DIRECTORY containing subdirectories (checkpoints, logs, outputs) and files\n- When os.remove() tried to delete a directory, it threw an exception\n- The exception was caught and logged as \"skipped\", so the script appeared to run successfully\n\n**Fix**: Changed `os.remove(run_path)` to `shutil.rmtree(run_path)` and added `import shutil`\n\n### Bug 2: Incompatible timestamp format (Line 41)\n**Issue**: `datetime.fromisoformat()` doesn't support 'Z' timezone suffix in Python < 3.11\n- metadata.json files contain timestamps "]
[112.769794, "i", "like \"2024-01-30T18:15:00Z\"\n- The 'Z' suffix indicates UTC timezone\n- fromisoformat() raised ValueError on the 'Z' suffix\n- Exception was caught, function returned None, so no runs were considered for deletion\n\n**Fix**: Added `.replace('Z', '+00:00')` to convert 'Z' to a format fromisoformat() accepts\nAlso updated cutoff calculation to use `datetime.now(created_at.tzinfo)` for proper timezone-aware comparison\n\n## Results\n- Before: 2.1GB used in /data/experiments, 20 old runs present\n- After: 32KB used in /data/experiments, all 20 old runs deleted\n- Reclaimed: ~2GB of disk space\n- Script now properly deletes runs older than 30 days\n\n## Changes Made\n1. Line 10: Added `import shutil`\n2. Line 41: Added `created_at_str = created_at_str.replace('Z', '+00:00')`\n3. Line 56: Changed `datetime.now()` to `datetime.now(created_at.tzinfo)`\n4. Line 62: Changed `os.remove(run_path)` to `shutil.rmtree(run_path)`\n\nBackup of original script saved to: /home/user/ops/purge_old_runs.py.bak\nEOF\n"]
